[[Algeria]]n music is virtually synonymous with [[Raï]] among foreigners; the [[musical genre]] has achieved great popularity in North Africa and Europe, especially [[Morocco]], [[Tunisia]], [[France]], and [[Spain]], among others. For several centuries, Algerian music was dominated by styles inherited from [[Al-Andalus]], eventually forming a unique North African twist on these poetic forms. Algerian music came to include suites called [[nuuba]]at (singular ''nuuba'').  Later derivatives include [[Rubab (instrument)|rabaab]] and [[hawzii]].

